<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyansittha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1112/13</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kyansittha was king of Pagan from 1084 to about 1112, one of the most celebrated rulers of the Pagan Kingdom. A general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anawrahta">Anawrahta</a>, he crushed the rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nga-yaman-kan">Nga Yaman Kan</a> in which King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sawlu">Sawlu</a> was killed and then took the throne. He built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ananda-temple">Ananda Temple</a>, maintained Mon culture at court, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajakumar">Rajakumar</a> set up the Myazedi inscription in his memory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kyansittha.jpg" alt="Kyansittha" width="320" height="571" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: O.Mustafin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kyansittha-Ananda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
